answer	flat_map keeps keys sorted, so the range query is lower_bound + a contiguous walk. A hash table has no order and would need a full scan or a second index. You give up point-lookup speed: the hash table was ~1.5–14× faster per lookup in the bench (e.g. 3.2 vs 19.5 ns, 6×, at N=4,096; 11.7 vs 162.8 ns, 14×, at N=1M).
